/Title (This project uses various Data Structures and Algorithms, including HashMap, ArrayList, and Queue. A HashMap is used to map each event name \(Tech Fest, Music Night, and Sports Day\) to its registration records so that event details can be accessed quickly. An ArrayList stores the confirmed participants up to a limit of 50 seats per event, while a FIFO Queue manages the waiting list whenever an event becomes full.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 751 0 R
/Prev 809 0 R
/Next 850 0 R
>>
endobj
850 0 obj
<<
/Title (The system validates every event entered by the user and displays a helpful message when an invalid event name is entered. When a confirmed participant cancels a registration using their registration ID \(starting from REG101\), the first participant in the waiting queue is automatically promoted to confirmed status.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 751 0 R
/Prev 849 0 R
/Next 810 0 R
>>
endobj
851 0 obj
<<
/Title (An event registration counter is the central point during college festivals where students register for competitions and cultural activities. It must allocate seats fairly, track unique registration IDs accurately, and automatically fill vacant seats from a waiting list when cancellations occur.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 811 0 R
/Next 869 0 R
>>
endobj
852 0 obj
<<
/Title (The events supported in the project are Tech Fest, Music Night, and Sports Day, with each event having a capacity of 50 seats and registration IDs starting from REG101. File handling is used to store and retrieve records through a text file named events.txt, ensuring that registration records are maintained even after the program is closed.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 811 0 R
/Prev 870 0 R
/First 871 0 R
/Last 871 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
